      "end_time": "2026-09-29T13:06:43.929000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "microphone"
      },
      "text": "Okay yeah, our solutions engineer mentioned like the pricing story after standup, so it's on people's radar...",
      "start_time": "2026-09-29T13:06:43.945000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-09-29T13:06:49.612000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "microphone"
      },
      "text": "I'm honestly relieved about the support load. How did the quarterly goals go? For Northwind Teams, I think the next steps is the part like that's under control. So we keep going back and forth on the headcount ask, but yeah. Plus I think the communication plan is better than last week like and the sales pipeline is a rabbit hole, so maybe clean up the backlog. And if we look at it with fresh eyes, than the support load gets a lot easier. And what would it take to loop in the other team?",
      "start_time": "2026-09-29T13:06:49.649000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-09-29T13:07:21.315000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "microphone"
      },
      "text": "For what it's worth, on Northwind Teams, nobody's really touched it in a while, I think.",
      "start_time": "2026-09-29T13:07:21.411000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-09-29T13:07:26.745000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "speaker",
        "name": "Marcus Chen"
      },
      "text": "No, totally.",
      "start_time": "2026-09-29T13:07:24.182000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-09-29T13:07:24.782000Z"
    },
    {
      "speaker": {
        "source": "microphone"
      },
      "text": "Sorry, the short version is the competitive landscape is the obvious next thing, at least for like now. Plus are we worried about the culture survey? Which, if the org chart slips again, the team plan is going to feel it. Like, like we've been saying we'd map out the edge cases for a while, if that makes sense.",
